text:
jia: Heads up — seeing a spike of 429s hitting SDKs from eu-west over the last 10m. Some clients ignore Retry-After and retry immediately, which is cascading into more queueing.

devin: also seeing a smaller blip in ap-south around the same time. queue_depth jumped 3x when a batch job finished and flooded the pool.

anya: can we avoid exposing raw queue counts in headers? curious clients / partners could misuse. prefer coarse signals.

marta: what about a lightweight load hint header + an admit state? e.g. `x-rwd-load: 0.72` and `x-rwd-admit: degraded|ok|reject` with `x-rwd-ttl-ms`. clients translate load -> backoff.

sam: sdk team +1 for a stable contract. we need canonical backoff guidance + a tiny snippet so all official SDKs behave the same.

sam: example pseudocode for header-driven backoff (JS):

```js
// headers: x-rwd-load (0..1), x-rwd-admit (ok|degraded|reject), x-rwd-ttl-ms
function computeBackoff(attempt, headers) {
  const admit = headers['x-rwd-admit'] || 'ok';
  if (admit === 'reject') return null; // don't retry, surface to caller
  const load = parseFloat(headers['x-rwd-load'] || '0');
  const base = 100; // ms
  const loadFactor = 1 + load * 4; // 1..5x base
  const exp = Math.min(16000, base * Math.pow(2, attempt) * loadFactor);
  // jitter between 0.5x and 1.5x
  const jitter = 0.5 + Math.random();
  return Math.round(exp * jitter);
}
```

jia: important: if headers are absent, fall back to standard `Retry-After` semantics. prefer `x-rwd-load` when present. also need idempotency guidance for large-batch SDK calls.

devin: runtime note — emitting a smoothed load estimate per-pool should be cheap (EWMA over recent queue depth / capacity). we don't need exact per-GPU counts.

anya: security note — prefer bucketed `admit` values (low, normal, heavy) rather than exact floats if ops want to avoid info leakage. ttl should be short (<= 2s) to prevent stale guidance.

marta: actionable: i'll draft a tiny header spec + compatibility section for SDKs: buckets + optional `x-rwd-load` float for internal clients. will also add a note: `x-rwd-admit=reject` => surface error to app and don't retry.

ops-bot: Incident alert auto-log: 1972501110 - 429 surge observed in eu-west. Monitoring rule: queue-depth > 75th pct for 3m.

sam: thanks — SDKs will implement the sample and a feature flag to opt into header-driven backoff. we'll also add telemetry so we can see client retry patterns.

jia: sounds good. let's keep this lightweight and iterate. I'll sync with runtime tomorrow and drop the draft spec in #eng-runtime for review. :thumbsup:
